## Current coverage

**40 workloads · 160 size/repetition cases · 5 fresh processes per side and mode.** Both registered input sizes and 1/16 whole-workload repetitions are included. Every peer is an isolated, uninstrumented executable.

The tables report **process footprint**, including code, stacks, allocator retention and GC policy. They do not measure comparable cross-language live heaps. Floors use the same executable; peaks are never subtracted or converted into compiler-memory win counts.
